    "note": "A box naming `align: justify`, holding a paragraph that names nothing. `align` is self-only (§4.4), so it aligns the lines of the node that named it, and the box has none: the paragraph inside must be set exactly as it would be with no style at all. The property inherits in CSS and does not in the format, so a reader built on a browser will justify the paragraph unless it is stopped, and then one document says two things.",
